0,400 less than a secondary teacher","Halved \u2014 the 16-17 employment rate has more than halved since the 1990s","-40% \u2014 under-19 apprenticeship starts are near a historic low, about 40% below their early-2010s peak","80% \u2014 sustained destination rate for the 16-18 Level 3 cohort from FE colleges, the lowest of any setting, against 88% for mainstream schools"],"Deliver":["15% \u2014 of 18-year-olds are NEET; 34% are in higher education and 20% in work without education or training","10 per 100 \u2014 extra young people in work for every 100 supported through apprenticeships, the most effective youth employment intervention (wage subsidies: 3)","\u00a315 per \u00a31 \u2014 return on a Level 2 apprenticeship for 19-23 year olds; youth apprenticeships cost about \u00a311k each","+7-8 ppt \u2014 more likely to be continuously employed at 25 for Level 3 apprenticeship completers than similar peers with a Level 2 qualification","20% / 30% \u2014 of women and men respectively are financially worse off for going to university, with returns varying hugely by subject"]},"note":"From the Ready to Work sprint evidence pack (July 2026). Attribute to it. Risk factors are percentage-point increases in NEET rate, all else held constant."}}